==================================================================================
PARITY (web CommandConfirmDialog.tsx -> native), no scope narrowing
==================================================================================
  Data sources (web -> native P1/S8 seam):
    useTranslation -> CommandConfirmStrings facade (P1/S10), no literals.
    open / def     -> CommandConfirmSource pushes a CommandConfirmRequest (the
                      resolved def copy + countdown + confirmInput + loading).
    onConfirm      -> CommandConfirmController.confirm() (async; no dispatch in view).
    onClose        -> CommandConfirmController.cancel() (Cancel / close / Escape).
  Logic (verbatim ports, unit-tested):
    countdown = def.countdown ?? 0            -> initialRemaining (clamp >= 0).
    setInterval prev <= 1 ? 0 : prev - 1      -> decremented; driven by the ticker seam.
    !confirmInput (empty string falsy)        -> hasTypedGate.
    input.trim().toUpperCase() === confirmInput.toUpperCase() -> inputMatches
                                                 (whitespace/newline trim; uppercased).
    canConfirm = remaining===0 && match       -> canConfirm.
    disabled={!canConfirm} + loading          -> confirmDisabled = busy || !canConfirm.
    `${t('common.confirm')} (${remaining}s)`  -> confirmButtonTitle ({{label}}/{{seconds}}).
    t(def.confirmKey, 'Are you sure?')         -> messageText (localized default).
    reset on (re)open (useEffect)             -> resetFormIfNewRequest keyed by commandID.
    Escape -> onClose ; Enter -> onConfirm     -> .keyboardShortcut(.cancelAction) /
      (when canConfirm && !loading)              .defaultAction on the disabled-gated buttons.
  Composition (web Modal/form -> native):
    red-bordered Modal + AlertTriangle        -> TSGlassPanel + red statusDanger header chip.
    <h2> t(def.labelKey)                       -> header title (caller-resolved).
    <p> message                                -> danger-tinted message block (AlertTriangle).
    type-to-confirm <Input>                    -> TextField (no autocap, autocorrect off),
                                                 prompt = confirmInput, bound to model.typed.
    ghost Cancel                               -> TSButton(.ghost), Escape.
    danger Confirm (loading, (Ns), opacity-50) -> TSButton(.destructive, isLoading: busy)
                                                 .disabled(confirmDisabled).opacity, Return.
  Native widening (honest, documented): the web component is only ever rendered with a
  command + open; the native surface widens that into the prompt-required loading /
  empty / error / stale / offline envelopes (never a blank box, engineering guideline
  #6) and surfaces the live-state freshness chip + cached-data banner (ADR-013). The
  web `loading` prop is unified with the in-flight confirm seam as `isBusy`. Cancel /
  Escape stay ungated by `loading` (faithful to the web `onClose`, unlike the 0012
  sibling's busy-swallow). Tailwind classes were NOT ported; chrome is P1/S9 tokens
  (TSSpacing/TSRadius/Color.TS/Font.TS) via TSGlassPanel/TSFadeIn/TSButton.

==================================================================================
STATES (every state renders -- no hidden surfaces)
==================================================================================
  loading  -> CommandConfirmLoadingState (spinner + "Preparing...").
  empty    -> CommandConfirmEmptyState (ContentUnavailableView "Nothing to confirm")
              -- the native widening of the web "modal only opens with a command".
  error    -> CommandConfirmErrorState (QueryError-equivalent + Retry -> model.refresh()).
  stale    -> freshness chip "Stale" + connectivity banner + ONE guarded auto-refresh.
  offline  -> freshness chip "Offline" + banner; cached command kept; no refetch.
  content  -> the populated confirm form (message + optional type-to-confirm field +
              Cancel/Confirm with the live countdown; + inline reload error if a refresh
              failed while a cached command remains).
  Telemetry: model.start() emits P1/S11 view.opened surface="CommandConfirmDialog"
  (once, idempotent -- ModelTests proven).

